      "description": {
        "fun": "Geodude sits so still on mountain paths that people mistake it for a rock and step on it, which makes it wave its arms in anger. Geodude bash into each other to see whose body is harder, and the older they get, the smoother and rounder they become. Some people have even used Geodude in snowball fights, which, given how heavy they are, is a bad idea.",
        "guide": "A boulder-like Rock and Ground Pokémon with two muscular arms. It sits still on mountain paths, where it is easily mistaken for a rock. It evolves into Graveler, and its Alolan form is a magnetic Rock and Electric type.",
