        "zh-Hant": "隆隆岩"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Golem's shell is so tough even dynamite can't scratch it. Once a year it sheds it to grow bigger, and the old shell crumbles into soil that farmers spread on their fields. It can pull in its head and limbs and roll downhill blind, so mountain villages dig grooves to steer rolling Golem away from houses. It even blows itself up to leap from mountain to mountain.",
        "guide": "The final stage of Geodude's line, a large Rock and Ground Pokémon with a hard, shell-like rock body. It sheds its shell once a year to grow and can roll at high speed with its head and limbs tucked in. It evolves from Graveler when traded, and its Alolan form is a Rock and Electric type with a rock cannon on its back.",
        "tagline": "A rolling boulder that sheds its shell for fertiliser",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Golem (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Golem_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
